Some nginx configuration in deploy/compose/ditto/ and charts/openegiz/
is adapted from the Eclipse Ditto Helm chart (Eclipse Public License 2.0,
included in charts/openegiz/LICENSE).

The legacy subcharts are preserved in the v1 archive under their original
licenses:

  Eclipse Ditto chart, Eclipse Hono chart  - Eclipse Public License 2.0
  Grafana chart, Bitnami MongoDB chart     - Apache License 2.0
  InfluxDB2 and Telegraf charts            - MIT License (InfluxData helm-charts)
  Mosquitto chart                          - ERTIS Research Helm-charts

The Extended API (services/extended-api/) is maintained first-party by
OpenEgiz. It was adopted from the ERTIS Research Group project

  Extended API for Eclipse Ditto
  Copyright ERTIS Research Group, University of Malaga
  https://github.com/ertis-research/extended-api-for-eclipse-ditto
  (adopted at commit b49663dea326854a2323423eaeab7e7f54d325a7)

The upstream repository ships no LICENSE file; its package.json declares the
ISC license. The source and runtime image include the ISC license and
ERTIS attribution (services/extended-api/LICENSE). OpenEgiz maintains the sources
first-party from `v2.0.0` on (git history records every change), and
publishes them in the platform's container images.

Eclipse Ditto, Grafana, InfluxDB, Telegraf, Eclipse Mosquitto and MongoDB
container images are pulled from their publishers at install time and are
covered by their own licenses.
